{"ref":"BDB, צָמֵא²","hw":"צָמֵא²","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">צָמֵא</span></big>  <strong>adj. thirsty</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 21:14\" href=\"/Isaiah.21.14\">Is 21:14</a> +; fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">צְמֵאָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 29:18\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.29.18\">Dt 29:18</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">צְמֵאִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 107:5\" href=\"/Psalms.107.5\">ψ 107:5</a>;—<em>thirsty</em>, usually + (or ‖) <span dir=\"rtl\">רָעֵב</span>: <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:29\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.29\">2 S 17:29</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 25:21\" href=\"/Proverbs.25.21\">Pr 25:21</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 107:5\" href=\"/Psalms.107.5\">ψ 107:5</a>, as subst. <em>thirsty one</em> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 29:8\" href=\"/Isaiah.29.8\">Is 29:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 32:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.32.6\">32:6</a>; so also <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 21:14\" href=\"/Isaiah.21.14\">21:14</a>, and (fig. of thirst for <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>’s favour) <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 55:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.55.1\">55:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">צָמֵא</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 44:3\" href=\"/Isaiah.44.3\">44:3</a> = <em>thirsty place</em> (Gunk<sup>l.c.</sup> proposes <span dir=\"rtl\">צְמֵאָה</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרָוָה אֶת־הַצְּמֵאָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 29:18\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.29.18\">Dt 29:18</a> <em>the watered</em> (plant, herbage) <em>with the thirsty</em>, fig. of <em>entire</em> people.","next":"BDB, צִמְאָה","prev":"BDB, צָמָא"}